IMPORT prelude

-- Stamp Duties Act 1929 (Singapore) -- stamp duty on buying and selling property under the First Schedule, Article 3: buyer's stamp
-- duty (paragraph (a)(iv), from 15 February 2023), additional buyer's stamp duty on residential property (paragraph (bi), from
-- 27 April 2023), seller's stamp duty on residential property (paragraphs (bg) and (bj)), and duty on shares (paragraph (c)).
--
-- Edition: 2021 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 October 2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SDA1929.txt, with amendments to 2025 shown (the 4 July 2025 seller's duty change). THE FIRST SCHEDULE TABLES ARE COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt DEPOSIT: the
-- percentages were matched to their bands by order of appearance (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6% residential; 1, 2, 3, 4, 5% non-residential),
-- not by line position.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to Article 3 duty on property sales and
-- share transfers, and (added for REQ-0008) Article 8 leases with the Third Schedule liability. Not encoded: the charging
-- and procedural provisions, mortgages, settlements, the
-- equity-interest provisions for property-holding entities, ABSD remission (s 15 and rules), and the joint-buyer elections.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Stamp Duties Act 1929 -- property`

§§ `First Schedule Article 3(a)(iv) -- buyer's stamp duty`

-- For instruments executed on or after 15 February 2023. Residential part: 1% of the first $180,000, 2% of the next $180,000, 3% of
-- the next $640,000, 4% of the next $500,000, 5% of the next $1,500,000, 6% above $3,000,000. Any remainder (non-residential): 1%,
-- 2%, 3%, 4% on the same first four bands, then 5% above $1,500,000.
-- Head-note: duty is "rounded down to the nearest dollar ... subject to a minimum stamp duty of $1". (Rounding is not modelled; the
-- cases use prices that give whole dollars.)
GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER, `width` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the slice` MEANS
    IF `price` AT MOST `from` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `price` MINUS `from` GREATER THAN `width` THEN `width` ELSE `price` MINUS `from`

GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residential buyer's stamp duty` MEANS
        `the slice` `price` 0 180000 TIMES 1 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 180000 180000 TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 360000 640000 TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 1000000 500000 TIMES 4 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 1500000 1500000 TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 3000000 1000000000000 TIMES 6 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-residential buyer's stamp duty` MEANS
        `the slice` `price` 0 180000 TIMES 1 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 180000 180000 TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 360000 640000 TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 1000000 500000 TIMES 4 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `price` 1500000 1000000000000 TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `First Schedule Article 3(bi) -- additional buyer's stamp duty`

-- For instruments executed on or after 27 April 2023, one residential property bought by a single buyer:
--   Singapore citizen owning no property -- no paragraph applies (no ABSD);
--   (iii) citizen owning one -- 20%;  (x) citizen owning two or more -- 30%;
--   (i) permanent resident owning none -- 5%;  (v) PR owning one -- 30%;  (xvi) PR owning two or more -- 35%;
--   (xvii) housing developer -- 40%;  (xviii) foreigner -- 60%;  (xix) trustee or entity -- 65%.
-- For joint buyers each paragraph applies only where "none of the other" joint buyers is in a higher-rate profile, so the
-- HIGHEST-rate buyer's profile governs. (The two-property elections in (ii), (iv), (vi) to (ix) are not modelled.)
DECLARE Buyer IS ONE OF
    `citizen owning none`
    `citizen owning one`
    `citizen owning two or more`
    `PR owning none`
    `PR owning one`
    `PR owning two or more`
    `housing developer`
    `foreigner`
    `entity or trustee`

GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Buyer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ABSD rate in percent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the buyer`
    WHEN `citizen owning none` THEN 0
    WHEN `citizen owning one` THEN 20
    WHEN `citizen owning two or more` THEN 30
    WHEN `PR owning none` THEN 5
    WHEN `PR owning one` THEN 30
    WHEN `PR owning two or more` THEN 35
    WHEN `housing developer` THEN 40
    WHEN `foreigner` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE 65

GIVEN `first buyer` IS A Buyer, `second buyer` IS A Buyer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the joint ABSD rate in percent` MEANS
    IF `the ABSD rate in percent` `first buyer` GREATER THAN `the ABSD rate in percent` `second buyer`
    THEN `the ABSD rate in percent` `first buyer`
    ELSE `the ABSD rate in percent` `second buyer`

GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Buyer, `price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total duty on a home purchase` MEANS
    `the residential buyer's stamp duty` `price` PLUS (`price` TIMES `the ABSD rate in percent` `the buyer` DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `First Schedule Article 3(bg), (bj) -- seller's stamp duty`

-- (bg): residential property acquired on or after 11 March 2017 but before 4 July 2025 and sold within 1 year -- 12%; within 2 years
-- -- 8%; within 3 years -- 4%.
-- (bj): acquired on or after 4 July 2025 -- 16%, 12%, 8%, and 4% within 4 years.
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD; holding periods are in years (a holding of exactly 1 year is "within one year").
GIVEN `acquired on` IS A NUMBER, `years held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the SSD rate in percent` MEANS
    IF `acquired on` AT LEAST 20250704
    THEN (IF `years held` AT MOST 1 THEN 16 ELSE IF `years held` AT MOST 2 THEN 12 ELSE IF `years held` AT MOST 3 THEN 8 ELSE IF `years held` AT MOST 4 THEN 4 ELSE 0)
    ELSE IF `acquired on` AT LEAST 20170311
         THEN (IF `years held` AT MOST 1 THEN 12 ELSE IF `years held` AT MOST 2 THEN 8 ELSE IF `years held` AT MOST 3 THEN 4 ELSE 0)
         ELSE 0

§§ `First Schedule Article 3(c) -- shares`

-- (c)(ii): a transfer on sale of stocks or shares executed on or after 22 February 2014 -- 0.2% of the consideration.
GIVEN `consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty on a share transfer` MEANS
    `consideration` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 1000

§§ `First Schedule Article 8 and Third Schedule Article 4 -- leases`

-- Added for REQ-0008 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl, cradle-to-grave-simone e054): a two-year tenancy of a flat at $2,400 a
-- month from June 2029 -- what duty, and who pays.
-- Article 8(aa): a lease or agreement for a lease "Without premium and executed on or after 22 February 2014": where the lease
-- is "Not exceeding 4 years", 0.4% of "the total rent and other consideration payable for the period of the Lease"; where it
-- is "Exceeding 4 years or for any indefinite term", "0.4% x A x 4 where A is the average rent and other consideration
-- calculated for a whole year". (The table is column-shifted in the .txt deposit; the formulas were read from their cells.)
-- Exemptions: 1. a lease under (a), (aa) or (c) executed on or after 1 April 2003 "where the average rent and other
-- consideration calculated for a whole year does not exceed $1,000"; 3. a lease under (a) or (aa) executed on or after 1 June
-- 2012 "in respect of the direct leasing of a flat from the Housing and Development Board under a scheme known as the 'Public
-- Rental Scheme'". (Exemption 2, a lease executed under a duly stamped agreement, is not modelled.)
-- Head-note: "the amount of proper stamp duty is to be rounded down to the nearest dollar ... subject to a minimum stamp duty
-- of $1 per instrument".
-- Third Schedule Article 4: for a "LEASE or AGREEMENT FOR A LEASE -- Article 8", the person liable to pay is "The lessee".
DECLARE Lease HAS
    `monthly rent` IS A NUMBER
    `term in months` IS A NUMBER
    `indefinite term` IS A BOOLEAN
    `direct HDB public rental` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average annual rent` MEANS
    `the lease`'s `monthly rent` TIMES 12

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is exempt` IF
        `the average annual rent` `the lease` AT MOST 1000
    OR  `the lease`'s `direct HDB public rental`

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty before rounding` MEANS
    IF `the lease`'s `indefinite term` OR `the lease`'s `term in months` GREATER THAN 48
    THEN `the average annual rent` `the lease` TIMES 4 TIMES 4 DIVIDED BY 1000
    ELSE `the lease`'s `monthly rent` TIMES `the lease`'s `term in months` TIMES 4 DIVIDED BY 1000

GIVEN `the lease` IS A Lease
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stamp duty on the lease` MEANS
    IF `the lease is exempt` `the lease`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (`the duty before rounding` `the lease`) LESS THAN 1
         THEN 1
         ELSE FLOOR (`the duty before rounding` `the lease`)

GIVETH A STRING
`who pays the duty on a lease` MEANS "the lessee"
